John Gibson <jgibsonNO@SPAMshakethebaby.com> wrote in 
news:agjqc.68390$QF3.62591@newssvr25.news.prodigy.com:

> A group of Stone giants appeared while I was clearing out Sokoban. 
> Although they did not disturb any of the existing boulders, a few of 
> them were generated with boulders of their own.  Naturally when I killed 
> them I was left with an unsolvable puzzle (until I smashed a boulder or 
> two).  Is this the intended behavior (forcing the player to take a luck 
> penalty)?

Nobody (except yourself) forced you to take a luck penalty.

For a start, you could have gone to Sokoban while still too low an 
experience level for giants to be generated. Most people do, most of the 
time, so giants aren't a big issue. If you choose to wait until you have 
reached a high experience level, then you should be prepared to deal with 
the consequences.

Even once the giants appeared, nobody forced you to kill them. Nor did they 
force you to kill them in a location that would leave the level unsolvable.

Even after you killed them you could have used a wand of teleport without 
penalty.

And without a wand of teleport, nobody forced you to finish Sokoban, you 
could have just walked away with your luck preserved.

